Finding: {"title":"Fail-open tenant check in aircraft logbook routes when org resolution returns null","severity":"HIGH","area":"Security / Multi-Tenant Isolation","files":["src/server/routes/routes-aircraft-logbook.ts"],"detail":"Two tenant guards fail OPEN instead of closed: (1) line 119 `verifyLogbookTenant`: `if (userOrgId && lb.flightSchoolId !== userOrgId) throw new Error('FORBIDDEN')` — when `userOrgId` is null/falsy, the whole condition short-circuits false and the check is skipped entirely. (2) line 174 in the `/aircraft-logbook/:equipmentId/logbooks` handler: `if (userOrgId && aircraft.flightSchoolId !== userOrgId) return 403` — same pattern. `resolveOrgIdFromSession` → `resolveOrgIdFromEmail` (helpers.ts:275-305) legitimately returns `null` whenever an authenticated user's email doesn't resolve to a row in `users` or `team_members` (e.g. deactivated account, onboarding race, data drift) — this is a real, reachable state, not merely theoretical.","impact":"An authenticated user whose session doesn't resolve to any org membership can view/modify ANY flight school's aircraft maintenance logbooks, entries, and amendments (FAA Part 43 compliance records) — since both guards silently let the request through when `userOrgId` is null instead of denying it.","recommendation":"Invert both checks to fail closed: `if (!userOrgId || lb.flightSchoolId !== userOrgId) throw/return 403`. Apply the same fix pattern anywhere else `if (userOrgId && ...)` is used as a tenant gate.","confidence":"high"}
confirmed=true only if the defect genuinely exists. If misread → verdict="false-positive". If real but wrong severity → set correctedSeverity. If real but underspecified → verdict="needs-detail" (kept). Return JSON per the schema.

